      "side": 1,
      "message": "With the changes I have locally, this fails. The reason why is because project tree D, E, and F already exists. Which means by default they are assuming the registered limit default of 10 volumes.\n\nWhen processing this request, the limit for D should fail because it\u0027s lower than the established registered limit. According to the specification, it should be possible to create a *new* project tree with D being the parent and having a project specific override of 9. This works in theory because it doesn\u0027t have any children assuming the registered limit to fail on (last example here [0]).\n\n[0] http://specs.openstack.org/openstack/keystone-specs/specs/keystone/rocky/strict-two-level-enforcement-model.html#enforcement-diagrams",
